  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Girraj vs State Of U.P. on 6 October, 2023 Author: Vivek Varma Bench: Vivek Varma High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2023:Ahc:195359 Court No. - 74 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 39130 of 2023 Applicant :- Girraj Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Rajiv Kumar Pandey Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Vivek Varma,J. 1.",
    "facts": "The instant bail application under Section 439 Cr.P.C. has been filed with the prayer to enlarge the applicant on bail in S.T. No. 282 of 2006, arising out of Case Crime No. 134 of 2003, under Sections 420, 272, 273 I.P.C. and 7/12 Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, Police Station Atrauli, District Aligarh during the pendency of the trial. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that earlier the applicant was granted bail by the trial Court on 24.09.2003. Though the applicant participated in the trial till 2021, the trial could not conclude and at the same time due to unavoidable reasons the applicant had left the station to earn livelihood. As such the applicant was reported to have absconded and has surrendered again on 01.08.2023 and since then he is in jail.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant on the basis of instructions submits that if the applicant is enlarged on bail, he shall appear regularly before the court below and shall not leave the station without permission of the court concerned. 5. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail but could not satisfactorily dispute the aforesaid submissions from the record.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant on the basis of instructions submits that if the applicant is enlarged on bail, he shall appear regularly before the court below and shall not leave the station without permission of the court concerned. 5. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail but could not satisfactorily dispute the aforesaid submissions from the record.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
